    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0145",
      "reading_order": 147,
      "section": "START CONTROL AT SET",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5654,
        "t": 565.3594068359375,
        "r": 291.552,
        "b": 517.4597492035388
      },
      "content": "The set is started with a Start/Stop/Preheat switch on the front panel of the DC control box. Component references are found on wiring/schematic diagrams in the Wiring Diagrams section of this manual.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_146",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_146",
          "title": "START CONTROL AT SET"
        }
      ],
      "page": 11,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0146",
      "reading_order": 148,
      "section": "START CONTROL AT SET",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 47.5654,
        "t": 502.71330683593754,
        "r": 291.45080000000036,
        "b": 442.2285492035389
      },
      "content": "The DC control box does not contain meters and is designed for remote mounting within limits of the wire harness (approximately 32 inches [813 mm]). An  optional  remote  control  panel  with  meters  is available in a kit from Cummins.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_146",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
