      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 676.0049068359375,
        "r": 440.6818,
        "b": 665.1856469606777
      },
      "content": "Control Components",
      "level": 2,
      "section_id": "sec_auto_154",
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_154",
          "title": "Control Components"
        }
      ],
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "page": 11,
      "chunk_hint": "section_heading",
      "semantic_role": "section_heading",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0153",
      "reading_order": 155,
      "section": "Control Components",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 653.6303068359375,
        "r": 564.7436999999995,
        "b": 631.0724492035388
      },
      "content": "The following describes the basic engine control components and how they function.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_154",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_154",
          "title": "Control Components"
        }
      ],
      "page": 11,
      "chunk_hint": "section_start",
      "semantic_role": "overview",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0154",
      "reading_order": 156,
      "section": "Control Components",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9386,
        "t": 618.2543068359375,
        "r": 564.9351000000006,
        "b": 557.7695492035389
      },
      "content": "A11 Engine Monitor Circuit Board: A circuit board that monitors the engine control system functions. This includes starting, stopping, and fault system operation.  Terminals are included for making remote connections.  See Figure 3-1.",
      "hyperlink_hint": true,
      "section_id": "sec_auto_154",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_154",
          "title": "Control Components"
        }
      ],
      "page": 11,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0155",
      "reading_order": 157,
      "section": "Control Components",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.93860000000006,
        "t": 544.9514068359376,
        "r": 564.7425999999992,
        "b": 522.3935492035389
      },
      "content": "Two relays soldered into the engine monitor board are not serviceable.  They function as follows:",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_154",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_154",
          "title": "Control Components"
        }
      ],
      "page": 11,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0156",
      "reading_order": 158,
      "section": "Control Components",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 330.7465,
        "t": 509.94560683593744,
        "r": 564.7627999999995,
        "b": 474.31624920353875
      },
      "content": " Power relay K12 connects battery B+ to the control meters and fuel solenoid during operation.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_154",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_154",
          "title": "Control Components"
        }
      ],
      "page": 11,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0157",
      "reading_order": 159,
      "section": "Control Components",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 330.7465,
        "t": 461.92670683593747,
        "r": 564.8639999999992,
        "b": 388.37044920353884
      },
      "content": " Starter  protection  relay  K15  is  AC  operated. When the Start switch is pressed, B+ is connected to K11 start solenoid through the K15 NC contacts until the generator output reaches about 90 volts AC.  At this voltage K15 activates and disconnects the starter circuit.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_154",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_154",
          "title": "Control Components"
        }
      ],
      "page": 11,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0158",
      "reading_order": 160,
      "section": "Control Components",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.93899999999996,
        "t": 375.5523068359376,
        "r": 564.7825999999991,
        "b": 315.06754920353893
      },
      "content": "K11 Start Solenoid: Located over the engine monitor circuit board (above K13 glow plug heater solenoid).  It connects battery B+ to the start solenoid, K13 heater solenoid, fuel solenoid and meters during cranking.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_154",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_154",
          "title": "Control Components"
        }
      ],
      "page": 11,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0159",
      "reading_order": 161,
      "section": "Control Components",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.93899999999996,
        "t": 302.2494068359377,
        "r": 565.0091999999994,
        "b": 254.40694920353894
      },
      "content": "K13 Glow Plug Heater Solenoid: Located directly above the monitor circuit board.  Connects B+ to the engine glow plugs during cranking.  It is energized by K11 start solenoid.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_154",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_154",
          "title": "Control Components"
        }
      ],
      "page": 11,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0160",
      "reading_order": 162,
      "section": "Control Components",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.93899999999996,
        "t": 241.5888068359377,
        "r": 564.7605999999993,
        "b": 206.388649203539
      },
      "content": "K14 Fuel Solenoid: It opens the fuel control valve when the  start/stop  switch  is  placed  in  the  Start position.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_154",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_3",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_3",
          "title": "3. Engine Controls"
        },
